    "b-70-container-isolation-code-4": {
      "id": "b-70-container-isolation-code-4",
      "type": "code",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "prepare → container (root mounted read-only, overlay upper on a per-run volume)\n   claude + bash/script nodes all run INSIDE via `docker exec`\n   env = the Archon-managed bag + auth only (never the host process.env)\n        │\n   … approval gate?  →  docker stop (0 RAM while stopped)  →  approve/resume → docker start\n        │\n   nodes done → WRITE-BACK GATE: overlay diff summarized, run pauses\n        │\n   approve → diff applied to the live root → run completed\n   reject  → diff discarded, live root untouched → run completed (noted)\n        │\n   teardown → container + volume removed"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-70-container-isolation-the-diagram-shows-a-norm-5": {
      "id": "b-70-container-isolation-the-diagram-shows-a-norm-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The diagram shows a normal gate pause. Failed resume setup or suspension can leave the container running; see "
        },
        {
          "insert": "Pause economics",
          "attributes": {
            "link": "#pause-economics"
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-70-container-isolation-the-overlay-s-upper-laye-6": {
      "id": "b-70-container-isolation-the-overlay-s-upper-laye-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The overlay's upper layer "
        },
        {
          "insert": "is",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " the diff by overlayfs construction, so computing what changed is a directory walk, not a tree comparison. Claude nodes run via the SDK's "
        },
        {
          "insert": "spawnClaudeCodeProcess",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " hook into "
        },
        {
          "insert": "docker exec",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "; "
        },
        {
          "insert": "bash:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "/"
        },
        {
          "insert": "script:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " nodes exec in the same container rather than silently falling back to host execution."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
