    },
    "b-70-container-isolation-pause-economics-20": {
      "id": "b-70-container-isolation-pause-economics-20",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Pause economics"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-70-container-isolation-on-a-normal-pause-inclu-21": {
      "id": "b-70-container-isolation-on-a-normal-pause-inclu-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "On a normal pause, including unreadable-source recovery before or inside the DAG, an approval/interactive gate mid-run, or the write-back gate at the end, Archon "
        },
        {
          "insert": "docker stop",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "s the container",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Once stopped, a multi-day wait costs ~0 CPU/RAM. Failed resume setup or suspension can leave the container running, as described below. Approve/reject/resume rediscover the container by its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "diy.archon.env-id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " label and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "docker start",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " it (or recreate one over the persisted upper volume if the container is gone). If the volume itself is gone (the only place the un-applied work lived), resume "
        },
        {
          "insert": "fails loudly",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rather than silently restarting from an empty overlay."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-70-container-isolation-the-cli-acquires-the-run-22": {
      "id": "b-70-container-isolation-the-cli-acquires-the-run-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The CLI acquires the run's authoritative resume claim before restarting its container, including write-back-only continuations. A stale or competing attempt that loses admission cannot restart or suspend the container. If restart or container credential setup fails before execution, the engine marks the admitted run failed and surfaces the setup error. The overlay and write-back decision remain available for ordinary failed-run resume; the prior pause reason is cleared and failed nodes replay on retry. During setup, SIGINT and SIGTERM wait for the in-flight operation to settle, then fail the admitted run before exiting with an error. Setup can fail or be interrupted after restart succeeds; in that case the container may remain running, and its overlay is preserved."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-70-container-isolation-unreadable-source-suspen-23": {
      "id": "b-70-container-isolation-unreadable-source-suspen-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Unreadable-source suspension uses a one-second Docker stop grace and a two-second timeout per Docker call (ownership restoration, stop, and failure inspection), keeping Docker work under the file store's ten-second lock wait. Other pauses retain Docker's default stop grace."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-70-container-isolation-stopping-is-best-effort-24": {
      "id": "b-70-container-isolation-stopping-is-best-effort-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Stopping is best-effort: a backend failure is logged and reported to the operator, and the run stays paused for retry. No "
        },
        {
          "insert": "container_stopped",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " event is emitted on failure; the container may keep consuming resources until resume or teardown."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-70-container-isolation-container-pauses-are-onl-25": {
      "id": "b-70-container-isolation-container-pauses-are-onl-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Container pauses are only resumable "
        },
        {
          "insert": "from the CLI",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", where the Docker backend is wired. Approving or rejecting a container run from chat or the Web UI records the decision but cannot continue the container. The run stays paused until you run "
        },
        {
          "insert": "archon workflow resume <run-id>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " from the CLI in the same project. Do not re-send the decision: the gate is already resolved."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-70-container-isolation-selection-and-configurat-26": {
      "id": "b-70-container-isolation-selection-and-configurat-26",
